1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,240
Stuck on a beach

2
00:00:01,280 --> 00:00:02,750
with only one tree,

3
00:00:02,790 --> 00:00:03,900
you'd sit under it.

4
00:00:03,940 --> 00:00:04,520
Don't.

5
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:05,890
It's a manchineel.

6
00:00:05,930 --> 00:00:07,510
It has small green apples,

7
00:00:07,550 --> 00:00:08,470
and a red band

8
00:00:08,510 --> 00:00:10,300
someone painted on the trunk.

9
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:12,140
Here's what that band is for.

10
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:13,080
A storm hits,

11
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:15,070
so you shelter under the leaves.

12
00:00:15,110 --> 00:00:16,880
Each one holds a milky sap,

13
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:18,030
and the rain drips it

14
00:00:18,070 --> 00:00:19,220
onto your skin.

15
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:21,400
Soon you're covered in blisters.

16
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:22,710
The next day you're starving,

17
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:24,440
and the apples smell good.

18
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:25,950
One bite is sweet,

19
00:00:25,990 --> 00:00:27,000
for a second.

20
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:28,380
Then your throat burns

21
00:00:28,420 --> 00:00:29,480
and tightens.

22
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:31,230
In Spanish, that fruit is

23
00:00:31,270 --> 00:00:33,110
the little apple of death.

24
00:00:33,150 --> 00:00:34,420
Later, nature calls,

25
00:00:34,460 --> 00:00:35,630
and you grab a handful

26
00:00:35,670 --> 00:00:36,930
of soft leaves.

27
00:00:36,970 --> 00:00:39,040
Same sap, same blisters,

28
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,640
much worse place.

29
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:41,950
That night you're cold,

30
00:00:41,990 --> 00:00:43,440
so you light its wood.

31
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:44,900
The smoke stings your eyes

32
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:46,710
until you can barely see.

33
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:47,500
Next time,

34
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:48,940
just sit in the sand.

35
00:00:48,980 --> 00:00:50,040
Subscribe for more

36
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:51,840
of nature's warnings.
